# Who may use Docker
- docker.sock is mounted on the scanner service only. The console calls the worker over HTTP with the scanner token.
- Do not mount the socket into Semgrep, Checkov, Trivy, or Sonar containers.
- The worker accepts only jobs that parse_job already allows. Do not add a passthrough for image, entrypoint, mounts, or env from the client.

```python
# Forbidden: the submitted image becomes the container
client.containers.run(user_image, ...)
# Required: pinned Trivy image, user ref is only an argument
client.containers.run(TRIVY_IMAGE, command=["image", image_ref], ...)
```

# Every scan container
- Image must be one of SEMGREP_IMAGE, CHECKOV_IMAGE, TRIVY_IMAGE, SONAR_IMAGE. Tags stay pinned.
- command and entrypoint are lists. privileged=False, cap_drop=["ALL"], no-new-privileges, mem_limit, nano_cpus, pids_limit.
- network_mode is scanner_network(). The value host is rejected.
- Semgrep and Checkov run as uid 65534 unless SCANNER_FORCE_ROOT=1. Trivy and Sonar keep the image user.
- read_only=True for Semgrep, Checkov, and Trivy. Sonar is the exception: read_only=False because the scanner writes under /tmp. Do not flip Sonar to read-only without a writable tmpfs that Java can actually use.
- Repo mounts are read-only. The Trivy cache volume is the only extra writable mount, and it is not the repo.
- Clean up containers and job directories in finally. Cap log size. Treat container logs as untrusted.
- Do not put the Sonar token in Config.Env or in argv. Keep the token-file plus shell wrapper in sonar_spec.
